# The sum of two balls with one-limb centers. The center is one rounded sum, whose error is at most
# U |cz| with U = unit_computed(add_1_1); a sum has no underflow error, so there is no V term.
kernel:        ball_add_1
input:         cx
input:         rx
input:         cy
input:         ry
output:        cz
output:        rz
value:         cx+cy
requires:      nonneg rx
requires:      nonneg ry
ensures:       encloses cz rz x+y x=cx,rx y=cy,ry
min_precision: 2
theorem:       proofs/theories/Ball.v ball_add_1_correct
source:        midpoint-radius sum (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
cone_exempt:   the radius never reaches the center; the special states of the ball layer (Milestone 1 statements, Ball kernels) test the center and the radii

cz = add(cx, cy)
mz = abs(cz)
d  = rmul(const unit_computed(add_1_1), mz)
r0 = radd(rx, ry)
rz = radd(r0, d)
